meta {
  name: Stream events for workflow
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/events/workflows?workflow_id={{workflowId}}
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  workflow_id: {{workflowId}}
}

headers {
  Accept: text/event-stream
}

docs {
  Same SSE stream, filtered to one workflow's events. All runs of that
  workflow contribute, but other workflows' events are dropped.

  `workflow_id` accepts a UUID only — not a workflow name (the SSE filter
  parses to UUID directly).

  A non-UUID `workflow_id` is silently treated as 'no filter' rather than rejected — paste a workflow name and you'll see all events.

  Unlike the run-filtered stream, `WorkflowChanged` events for the filtered workflow ARE included here (they carry a `workflow_id`).

  Each event is dispatched with a named SSE `event:` line in addition to the JSON `data:` payload. The names are snake_case: `run_started`, `step_started`, `step_output`, `step_completed`, `run_completed`, `run_failed`, `workflow_changed`.

  The server emits a 15-second SSE keep-alive comment (`:keepalive`). When the broadcast channel lags, it emits `: lagged: some workflow events were missed`. There is no server-side reconnect; clients use standard EventSource auto-reconnect.
}
